---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
---

<Page title="Privacy" description="Your files never leave your browser. What Animated SVG GO stores, and what it doesn't.">
  <div class="flex flex-col gap-8">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold">Privacy</h1>
    <p class="text-lg">Your files never leave your browser.</p>

    <section aria-labelledby="never-heading" class="flex flex-col gap-2">
      <h2 id="never-heading" class="text-xl font-bold">What we never do</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6">
        <li>Upload your files. Every step runs on your machine.</li>
        <li>Ask for an account, a name or an email.</li>
        <li>Use analytics, trackers or cookies.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="stored-heading" class="flex flex-col gap-2">
      <h2 id="stored-heading" class="text-xl font-bold">What stays in your browser</h2>
      <p>
        The last file you opened, and its effects, are saved in this browser's own storage so they're there when you come back. Only this
        browser on this machine can see them. Opening another file replaces them. To remove them, clear this site's data in your browser
        settings.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="hosting-heading" class="flex flex-col gap-2">
      <h2 id="hosting-heading" class="text-xl font-bold">Hosting</h2>
      <p>
        The site is hosted by <a class="link" href="https://vercel.com/legal/privacy-policy">Vercel</a>. Like any web host, it keeps standard
        request logs when you load a page, such as your IP address and browser. Your files are never in them, because they are never sent.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Page>
